00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:36.960
Where do you think you're
going at this time of day?

00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:39.590
Please let me pass.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:44.140
That's a Zhcted war maiden?

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:44.720
Yes.

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:48.680
Our mistress, Wind Princess of the Silver Flash,

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:53.810
also known as Danseuse of the Sword, 
Lady Eleonora Viltaria.

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:59.530
What? You don't like this outfit?

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:04.200
I changed into these clothes so you wouldn't have to look away, you know?

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:10.870
I have to go back to Alsace!

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:14.170
You're our prisoner, remember?

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:16.790
Thenardier's soldiers are on their way to Alsace!

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:18.790
I can't wait here until the town's destroyed!

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:19.800
Please let me go!

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:25.160
I will return the moment I'm done.
You have my word!

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:27.740
And just what do you plan
to do once you get to Alsace?

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.320
What am I—?

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:31.350
Defend my people, of course!

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:33.030
How?

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:34.830
H-How...?

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:37.260
I know you're an accomplished marksman.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:39.980
But you are also only one person.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.440
I'm not doubting your skill or resolve,

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:45.110
but standing alone against
an enemy of three thousand?

00:03:45.110 --> 00:03:46.240
It's a fool's errand.

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:47.950
I know that!

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:49.870
You know that, yet you're still going?

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.700
But I might...

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:53.500
I might be able to do something!

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:56.620
As if rushing in so haphazardly, 
without a plan, could help anyone!

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:02.630
I told you, deserters are put to the sword.

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:04.970
If you want to die that badly,

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:07.260
you might as well meet your end here.

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:12.520
It doesn't matter whether you perish in Leitmeritz or in Alsace.

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:16.900
Then you won't let me go, no matter what?

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:22.780
Do you even understand
what I'm so annoyed about?

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:25.820
Try and use your brain, would you?

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:31.030
Back in Dinant, you did all you could to try and gain an advantage.

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:33.160
But now you've lost control of your emotions

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:35.290
and are rushing ahead without thinking.

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:37.160
Concentrate on what you can do instead.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:39.920
Then what am I supposed to do?

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:51.050
<i>Why isn't Elen striking me down?</i>

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:55.600
<i>And she could easily order Rurick and the others to drag me back.</i>

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:00.060
Young Lord...

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:05.520
<i>Is Elen...</i>

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:09.300
<i>offering me a chance to save Alsace?</i>

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:16.660
I have a favor to ask.

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:17.680
Hm?

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:22.840
Please lend me your troops.

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:28.260
A prisoner... wants to be given soldiers?

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.540
Oh, wow...

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:02.630
That was downright refreshingly audacious.

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:11.300
You want to borrow my men?

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:12.380
Very well.

00:06:13.050 --> 00:06:14.800
But not for free, of course.

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:16.810
How much?

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:18.930
All of Alsace.

00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:21.560
As long as you promise to govern fairly

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:24.440
and to keep the residents safe...

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:27.610
That's all he wants in return, huh?

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:28.440
It's settled!

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:31.320
Raise the Zirnitra banners!

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:33.700
To battle!

00:06:50.270 --> 00:06:51.890
That came as a surprise.

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:54.390
I never thought he would
ask you to lend him troops.

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:57.720
Both of us had pegged him wrong, huh?

00:06:58.820 --> 00:07:02.690
You thought Tigre would challenge me to an archery contest.

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:07.440
And I assumed he'd ask to
become one of my subordinates.

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:11.730
You were unable to make him act the way you desired.

00:07:11.730 --> 00:07:14.260
Therefore you've lost this wager, Lady Eleonora.

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:16.460
And I did too.

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:19.080
It's hardly a bet if we both lose, is it?

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:22.040
He's here!

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:28.790
You're going into battle dressed like <i>that</i>?

00:07:28.790 --> 00:07:31.300
You <i>will</i> be leading an army, remember?

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:33.630
Well, that's all I have.

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:36.140
Hm...

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:38.470
What are we going to do with you?

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:41.470
There's no time left; you'll have to go like this.

00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:45.640
However, you could've at least combed your hair properly.

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:46.730
Well, I...

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:49.320
All right! Me, too!

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:52.360
Huh? L-Listen, I...

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:52.360
Here, come on!

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:55.860
Well, that's certainly better.

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:00.870
Hm? What's wrong?

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:02.660
I like the way you look at me,

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:05.080
but saying a word or two wouldn't hurt.

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:06.870
How about "You're beautiful"?

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:12.130
That's what I've been thinking ever since I first saw you at Dinant.

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:17.970
They've got three thousand men!

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:19.300
We have one thousand!

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:20.350
Do we stand a chance?!

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:22.720
They don't know the lay of the land!

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:27.690
I doubt anyone from the House of Thenardier has been in Alsace for quite some time!

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:30.900
I, on the other hand, am familiar with every hill and valley here!

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:32.230
So we can use the terrain to our advantage.

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:34.990
All right, let's win this!

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:47.040
That's it.

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:49.710
Slowly, so they get a good look.

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:52.750
You can side with House Thenardier or House Ganelon.

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:56.300
I hope you'll make the
right choice, people of Brune!

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:02.680
So the real reason you sent
Lord Zion to Alsace is...

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:05.680
Now that Prince Regnas has fallen in battle,

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:10.060
the king is losing his grip on the throne.

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:14.730
Soon Brune will be ruled either by me or Ganelon.

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:18.650
At some point we'll have to settle who it'll be.

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:22.230
Alsace...

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:24.910
There's nothing important about it.

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:27.200
It's Brune's most remote region.

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:31.460
However, it may fall into Ganelon's hand.

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:33.460
And you'd rather reduce it to ashes?

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:38.470
Still, sending three thousand soldiers to such a backwater place,

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:40.680
not to mention those two dragons...

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:43.220
The weak must be crushed completely.

00:09:44.050 --> 00:09:47.350
I also want Zion to get used to handling dragons.

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:51.100
Don't fall behind!

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:53.860
Hurry! Head for the mountains or the forest!

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:56.690
Everyone, to the temple!

00:09:56.690 --> 00:09:59.820
They're not going to desecrate it!

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:05.780
I'll stop Ganelon from mobilizing, one way or another.

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:09.290
Bertrand, go to Zhcted.

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:12.120
Let Tigre know what is happening.

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:13.670
Leave it to me.

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:16.380
I'll make sure to bring the young lord back with me.

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:19.550
Titta, you should help the soldiers with evacuating the townsfolk.

00:10:20.130 --> 00:10:22.720
Those strong enough will go to the mountains or the forest.

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:24.430
The others will take shelter in the temple.

00:10:25.050 --> 00:10:29.140
Not even Thenardier would risk making an enemy of all the temples throughout Brune.

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:30.060
Right!

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:32.140
Titta, what about you?

00:10:32.140 --> 00:10:34.350
Won't you take refuge outside the city?

00:10:34.350 --> 00:10:35.690
I'll be staying at the mansion.

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:40.440
I want to make sure there'll be someone to greet Lord Tigre when he returns.

00:11:09.970 --> 00:11:12.140
Every time I look at that bow, it's the same.

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:15.310
The pressure's overwhelming.

00:11:15.810 --> 00:11:17.860
You mustn't say that, Lord Tigre.

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:21.650
It is a precious family heirloom left to you by your ancestors.

00:11:21.650 --> 00:11:23.950
That's why I pay my respects every day.

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:26.070
Same as I did today. Like always.

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:30.540
It's been two years since my father died.

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:33.330
I'm still not much of a ruler,

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:34.960
but Bertrand is here

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:36.630
and so are you, Titta.

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:39.960
We wouldn't be doing nearly as well without you two.

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:43.590
Y-You're acting weird this morning!

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:45.470
It's not like you, Lord Tigre!

00:11:46.090 --> 00:11:47.220
Thanks.

00:11:48.260 --> 00:11:50.850
No! Please stop!

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:53.430
I want to see you off the usual way!

00:11:58.060 --> 00:11:59.610
The young lord will be here soon.

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:04.270
Though, I'm sure he's catching hell from Titta for oversleeping right about now.

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:08.090
Why?

00:12:08.090 --> 00:12:11.750
Why must you fight in this war, Lord Tigre?

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:14.350
His Majesty has called for us.

00:12:14.350 --> 00:12:18.670
I'm a count in the Kingdom of Brune and head of House Vorn, so that's how things work.

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:19.500
But...

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:22.670
It's all right. It's a huge army.

00:12:22.670 --> 00:12:25.340
And we're going to be placed back in the rear.

00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:26.510
I promise, I'm coming back.

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:39.150
Lord Tigre...

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:42.190
You're coming back.

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:45.860
You're coming back, aren't you, Lord Tigre?

